  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001025">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">located in</rdfs:label>
    <ns4:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">Location as a relation between instances: The primitive instance-level relation c located_in r at t reflects the fact that each continuant is at any given time associated with exactly one spatial region, namely its exact location. Following we can use this relation to define a further instance-level location relation - not between a continuant and the region which it exactly occupies, but rather between one continuant and another. c is located in c1, in this sense, whenever the spatial region occupied by c is part_of the spatial region occupied by c1.    Note that this relation comprehends both the relation of exact location between one continuant and another which obtains when r and r1 are identical (for example, when a portion of fluid exactly fills a cavity), as well as those sorts of inexact location relations which obtain, for example, between brain and head or between ovum and uterus</ns4:IAO_0000116>
    <ns4:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">Most location relations will only hold at certain times, but this is difficult to specify in OWL. See http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro/docs/temporal-semantics/</ns4:IAO_0000116>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <ns4:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">a relation between two independent continuants, the target and the location, in which the target is entirely within the location</ns4:IAO_0000115>
    <ns4:IAO_0000118 xml:lang="en">located_in</ns4:IAO_0000118>
    <ns4:IAO_0000233>add `Inverse Of`
issue https://github.com/OpenEnergyPlatform/ontology/issues/979
pull request https://github.com/OpenEnergyPlatform/ontology/pull/1086</ns4:IAO_0000233>
    <ns4:RO_0001900 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001901"/>
    <dc:source>http://www.obofoundry.org/ro/#OBO_REL:located_in</dc:source>
    <ns4:IAO_0000111 xml:lang="en">located in</ns4:IAO_0000111>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000004"/>
    <ns4:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">my brain is located in my head</ns4:IAO_0000112>
    <ns4:IAO_0000112 xml:lang="en">this rat is located in this cage</ns4:IAO_0000112>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
