    <rdfs:comment>The operation of a powered, aerial vehicle that does not carry a human operator.
Description:
A type of special air traffic. (NATO derived) An Unmanned Aerial Vehicle uses aerodynamic forces to provide vehicle lift, can fly autonomously or be piloted remotely, can be expendable or recoverable, and can carry a lethal or non-lethal payload.
