  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://data.nasa.gov/ontologies/atmontoCore">
    <owl:imports rdf:resource="https://data.nasa.gov/ontologies/atmonto/general"/>
    <owl:imports rdf:resource="https://data.nasa.gov/ontologies/atmonto/ATM"/>
    <owl:imports rdf:resource="https://data.nasa.gov/ontologies/atmonto/NAS"/>
    <owl:imports rdf:resource="https://data.nasa.gov/ontologies/atmonto/equipment"/>
    <owl:imports rdf:resource="https://data.nasa.gov/ontologies/atmonto/data"/>
    <dc:creator>Richard M. Keller</dc:creator>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology"/>
    <owl:versionInfo>1.0</owl:versionInfo>
    <dc:description>The ATM Ontology describes classes, properties, and relationships relevant to the domain of air traffic management, and represents information pertinent to a broad and diverse set of interacting components in the US and the global airspace, including flights, aircraft, manufacturers, airports, airlines, air routes, facilities, air traffic advisories, weather phenomena, and many others. There are three interrelated ontologies in the ATM Ontology suite: atmontoCore (https://data.nasa.gov/ontologies/atmontoCore), atmonto (https://data.nasa.gov/ontologies/atmonto), and atmontoPlus (https://data.nasa.gov/ontologies/atmontoPlus). The 'atmontoCore' ontology contains only classes and property definitions, but does not contain any class instances or property values. (This corresponds to the ATM Ontology's TBox, or terminological component.) The 'atmonto' ontology, which imports the 'atmontoCore' ontology, includes the aforementioned classes and property definitions, along with class instances and associated property values (i.e., TBox plus ABox fact assertions). In particular, the 'atmonto' ontology contains instances corresponding to relatively static, temporally-stable data pertaining to the US National AIrspace. Finally,the 'atmontoPlus' ontology imports the 'atmonto' ontology and adds additional instances covering a sample set of temporally-dependent flight, advisory, and weather data for the month of July 2014. (Due to volume considerations, only 100 flights from 15 July 2014 are included in this sample.) See the documentation at https://data.nasa.gov/ontologies/atmontoCore for further details.</dc:description>
    <dc:date>2018-03-20</dc:date>
    <dc:title>Air Traffic Management (ATM) Ontology: includes core classes and properties</dc:title>
    <dcterms:license rdf:resource="https://data.nasa.gov/ontologies/atmontoCore#ATMontologyLicenseTerms"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://openenergy-platform.org/ontology/oeo/OEO_00320048">
