    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UO_0000000"/>
    <ns4:IAO_0000600>A composed unit is composed of at least two other units. Examples are:
m/s has a linear numerator metre and a linear denominator second.
kg/m³ has a linear numerator kilogram and a cubed denominator metre.
Wh has two linear numerators: Watt and hour</ns4:IAO_0000600>
