    <ns4:IAO_0000600>A composed unit is composed of at least two other units. Examples are:
m/s has a linear numerator metre and a linear denominator second.
kg/m³ has a linear numerator kilogram and a cubed denominator metre.
Wh has two linear numerators: Watt and hour</ns4:IAO_0000600>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has unit numerator</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
    <ns4:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">A relation between a (composed) unit A and a unit B in which B is in the numerator of unit A.</ns4:IAO_0000115>
  </rdf:Description>
