    <dc:description>Employee: An Firm has some Employees, whom it employs for some Occupation.
An Employee is a type of Organization Agent.
An Employee may be employed at a particular Business Establishment.
An Employee may be responsible for one or more Roles within the Organization.
An Employee is employed by some Organization, unless the Person is self-employed.
An Employee has a Wage/Salary and may work at some Location (this may be the location of the Firm, an alternate Location, or a Location that is subject to change).</dc:description>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N6c7e2a1b42e140ff9e48a9bd99e81887"/>
  </rdf:Description>
