  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/airm-o/ontology#CodePointUsageType-FINAL_ROLL_OUT_POINT">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/airm-o/ontology#CodePointUsageType"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Where a course change is required within the Final Approach Segment (FAS), the point that the aircraft rolls to a wings-level attitude aligned with the runway centreline extended is considered the FROP.FROP is used in an RNP-SAAAR procedure when a turn is required in the final between the FAF and the threshold.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>FINAL_ROLL_OUT_POINT</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
