  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://ontology.eil.utoronto.ca/icity/PublicTransit/TransitIncident">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://ontology.eil.utoronto.ca/icity/PublicTransit/TransitOntologyThing"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N7dffb420cd4d445f88609f948d97a96f"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N14cdbfb2cd1541bc9c50f5b384f0bcc0"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N43edb2dabbc64a078ac0a48ac0815e4a"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="N1dcfb0700ac7473f84c541f52a14f989"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://ontology.eil.utoronto.ca/icity/Activity/Activity"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Transit Incidents are events of interest that occur on a particular transit trip. Typically, they are problematic, unplanned issues resulting in some delay.

A TransitIncident is a subclass of Activity.
It is associated with some station or stop point.
An incident may be described (and so classified) by a predefined code: hasCode only xsd:String.
An incident will have some resulting caused gap (i.e. the time from the incident until the next train arrives at the station).</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
