    <rdfs:comment>After analysis it appeared that the problem was not a real problem and does not require action to be solved. Note that if a Hotspot is really no longer required it is simply removed completely. The ACCEPTABLE state is solely intended to indicate that a Hotspot has been accepted as a problem that can be tolerated (e.g. no resolution action such as a STAM needs to be applied).</rdfs:comment>
