  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://ontology.eil.utoronto.ca/icity/LandUse/UnimprovedPasture">
    <dc:description>K - Unimproved pasture and range land </dc:description>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://ontology.eil.utoronto.ca/icity/LandUse/CLUMPClassification"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="Nb29feef7f93043bca1e4fed3748bb9ad"/>
    <rdfs:comment>'K' Rough grazing and range land. Areas of natural grasslands, sedges, herbaceous plants and abandoned farmland whether used for grazing or not. Bushes and trees may cover up to 25% of the area. Intermittently wet hay lands (sloughs or meadows) are included as long as the land is utilized. Within some grassy, open woodlands, bushes and trees may exceed 25% cover if the area is actively grazed and no other use dominates. </rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
