    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/airm-o/ontology#CodeFinalGuidanceType"/>
    <rdfs:comment>An LPV approach is classified as an APV procedure based on the lateral OCS dimensions of the precision approach trapezoid, with vertical guidance provided by the WAAS where the VAL is greater than 12 and less than or equal to 50 meters. These procedures are published on RNAV Global Positioning System (GPS) approach charts as the LPV minima line.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>LPV</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
